// #403 (F25): tsconfig.json next door is the BUILD config — it excludes `src/**/*.test.ts` so
// `tsc` doesn't emit test files into dist/. A side effect of that exclusion was that the test
// suites were never type-checked AT ALL (they run under tsx, which strips types without checking
// them), so the compiler could not be the enforcement mechanism for anything a fixture got wrong.
//
// It has to be, for #403's required-clock seams: "a fixture that omits the clock fails to
// compile" is only true if fixtures are compiled. This config is that check — same include set,
// noEmit, and a NAMED legacy exclusion list below.
//
// The legacy list is pre-existing type debt with nothing to do with clocks: each excluded file
// declares a partial `FakeForge`/`FakeMergeGate` double as `implements IForge` that never grew
// the members IForge grew (~1000 of the ~1100 errors are that one class of mistake, repeated per
// call site). The suites pass at runtime because tsx never checks them. Making those doubles
// whole is its own change, not #403's — so they stay excluded and NAMED rather than silently
// unchecked. `merge-driver.test.ts` and `reviewer.test.ts` additionally sit next to
// human-merge-only sources (docs/security.md), so their debt is a human's to clear.
//
// #403 DID clear every file whose only errors were incidental (missing optional-field fixtures,
// an `asserts actual is T` narrowing slip, an explicit-undefined under exactOptionalPropertyTypes)
// — which matters because that set includes every suite the clock sweep touched a date-seeded
// fixture in: worker.test.ts, peripheral.test.ts, decompose.test.ts, cli.test.ts, plus
// watchdog/materializer/logger/state, which were never excluded.
//
// The residual gap is honest and bounded: in a still-excluded file the compiler cannot catch a
// fixture that forgets `now`, but that fixture no longer falls back to the wall clock either —
// the production seams have no default left, so it fails LOUDLY at runtime ("now is not a
// function"), which is the actual property #403 needed. Compile-time is the earlier, better
// signal; runtime is the backstop.
//
// Shrink this list; never grow it. Deleting an entry (after fixing that file's errors) is always
// a safe change; adding one is a regression to argue about in review.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": [
    "src/loop/align.test.ts",
    "src/loop/cli-rounds.test.ts",
    "src/loop/conductor.test.ts",
    "src/loop/dissent.test.ts",
    "src/loop/driver.test.ts",
    "src/loop/escalation-reconcile.test.ts",
    "src/loop/harvest.test.ts",
    "src/loop/round-defaults.test.ts",
    "src/loop/round.test.ts",
    "src/proxy/mcp-server.test.ts",
    "src/retro/retro-digest.test.ts",
    "src/retro/retro.test.ts",
    "src/roles/architect.test.ts",
    "src/roles/merge-driver.test.ts",
    "src/roles/plan-review.test.ts",
    "src/roles/reviewer.test.ts"
  ]
}
